This paper explores the intersection of \LaTeX\ typesetting and the
digital humanities. More specifically, it asks why \LaTeX\ typesetting
is used so infrequently in the Digital Humanities (DH), despite its
clear advantages and applications.

This paper, on the one hand, aims to understand the reasons why \LaTeX\
isn't more widely used in the digital humanities and, on the other hand,
presents three examples of relevant use cases to illustrate its value
for the (Digital) Humanities.
